# Copy this file to .env.local (already git-ignored via the *.local rule)
# and fill in real values to enable the Google Drive reference picker under
# Project → References. Until both variables below are set, that feature
# shows a clear "Google Drive isn't connected" state — nothing is faked.
#
# Setup (Google Cloud Console):
#   1. Create or select a project.
#   2. Enable the "Google Drive API" and the "Google Picker API".
#   3. Credentials → Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID → Web application.
#      Add this app's origin(s) (e.g. http://localhost:5173) under
#      "Authorized JavaScript origins". Use that client ID below.
#   4. Credentials → Create API key → restrict it to the Picker API and to
#      this app's HTTP referrers. Use that key below.
#
# Neither value is a secret in the traditional sense (both are sent to the
# browser and are restricted by origin/API in the Cloud Console), but they
# are still specific to a deployment — never commit real values.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Cloud Foundation — auth, database, storage)
#
# Until both variables below are set, AURA runs in local-only mode: every
# existing feature works exactly as before, purely against localStorage,
# with no auth wall and no cloud sync. Setting them turns on Sign up/Sign in
# and background cloud sync — see docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md for the full setup
# walkthrough (creating the project, running migrations, configuring the
# storage bucket).
#
# Both values are safe to expose to the browser (the publishable/anon key is
# designed for client-side use and is meaningless without Row Level Security,
# which this project's migrations enable on every table) — but never commit
# a real value here, and NEVER put a service-role/secret key in this file or
# anywhere in frontend code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
